# Ownership is by domain directory, which is why the tree is shaped this way.
#
# These paths are the review boundary for a change to a tool's SHAPE. They are
# not sufficient for a change to its POLICY — see README.md: a clearance or
# compartment edit looks like an ordinary proto diff, and a domain owner is not
# a security reviewer. That gap wants a policy diff in CI, not more owners.

/proto/accounts/    @bank/retail-accounts
/proto/cards/       @bank/cards
/proto/payments/    @bank/payments
/proto/screening/   @bank/financial-crime

# The shared taxonomy. Every domain depends on it and no domain owns it, so it
# gets an explicit owner rather than defaulting to whoever reviews fastest.
/proto/bank/        @bank/security-architecture

# The vendored annotations are written verbatim by `garm init`. A diff here is
# either an upgrade or a mistake, and both want the same eyes.
/third_party/       @bank/security-architecture
